[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-30
TITLE: Control loop - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is operating with grid control enabled, the firmware shall
adjust the grid output in response to the difference between requested and
measured emission current while keeping the output within its configured limits.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A treatment plan should be ready to load.
* Grid control is enabled.
* Instruments are connected to observe emission-current feedback and grid output.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Load a treatment plan.
3. Record the requested emission-current setpoint.
4. Start the emission.
5. Record the measured emission-current feedback and grid output.
6. Observe the feedback error and subsequent grid-output commands.
7. Repeat with different approved operating setpoints.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
3. Verify the requested setpoint is reported correctly.
4. Verify the emission started.
5. Verify emission feedback and grid output are available.
6. Verify grid output changes in response to the feedback error.
7. Verify the grid output remains within its configured minimum and maximum.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-14
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-31
TITLE: PC Communication 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered on, the user can send a request through firmware to run bootloader
application and load a new set of firmware through the USB.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* Bootloader application should be loaded in the USB and should be present for user to run it.
* A new set of firmware should be in the USB.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Run bootloader application through USB.
3. Click Logs symbol in the left-hand side of screen.
4. Check the utility log.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully and there is not any treatment plan loaded into system.
2. Verify the application started to run.
3. Verify the logs displayed in the middle of screen.
4. Record the utility log and verify system enters into bootloader mode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-19
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-32
