2. Run bootloader application through USB.
3. Click Logs symbol in the left-hand side of screen.
4. Check the utility log.
5. Check the USB free space.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully and there is not any treatment plan loaded into system.
2. Verify the application started to run.
3. Verify the logs displayed in the middle of screen.
4. Record the utility log and verify system enters into bootloader mode.
5. Verify an area in the USB which was corresponded to application CRC verification area was erased.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-19
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-38
TITLE: PC Communication 3 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered on, the user can send a request through firmware to get or set any configuration parameters.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* The USB connection is established between the PC and the HVPS board
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Navigate to the Service page
3. Select a configuration parameter and enter a new value.
4. Save or apply the new value.
5. Verify that the displayed value matches the value entered in Step 3.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system accepts the new value entered for the selected configuration parameter.
2. Verify the system updates the configuration parameter successfully.
3. Verify the displayed value matches the value entered by the user.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-19
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-39
TITLE: PC Communication 4 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered on, the user can send a request through firmware to retrieve all configuration values, setpoints, or feedback values in a single bulk-read response.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* The USB connection is established between the PC and the HVPS board
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Navigate to the Service page.
3. Issue a bulk-read request for all configuration values.
4. Verify that all returned configuration values match the currently stored values on the device.
5. Issue a bulk-read request for all setpoints.
6. Verify that all returned setpoint values match the currently stored values on the device.
7. Issue a bulk-read request for all feedback values.
8. Verify that all returned feedback values match the currently stored values on the device.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system accepts each bulk-read request.
2. Verify the system returns a single response frame containing all values for the requested parameter category, packed sequentially in index order.
3. Verify the returned values match the currently stored values on the device for each category (configuration values, setpoints, feedback values).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-19
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-33
TITLE: Filament current ramping - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The user powered on the system, loaded a treatment plan. Then after warmup procedure, user has
to make sure the warm up is logged in the system.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A treatment plan is ready to load.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Load a treatment plan.
3. Check the state of the system.
4. Wait till the Warmup procedure is finished.
5. Click the Logs symbol in the left side of the screen.
6. Check the logs.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
3. Verify its state is Warmup.
4. Verify the status of the system is not Warmup anymore.
5. Verify the logs displayed in the screen.
6. Verify the log for readings of the filament current ramp up during the warmup procedure. Values in the log should indicate a ramp rate of less than 1A/sec.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-8
  ROLE: Verifies

