[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-35
TITLE: External ADC feedback acquisition - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall acquire high-voltage and cathode-current feedback through
the external ADC interfaces and publish valid paired feedback results.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A calibrated external signal source or suitable HVPS test fixture is connected.
* A logic analyzer or oscilloscope can observe both external ADC interfaces.
* The feedback display or approved diagnostic trace is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Observe both external ADC chip-select signals and SPI activity.
3. Capture a complete feedback acquisition sequence.
4. Verify that both feedback channels are acquired through DMA.
5. Record the published high-voltage and cathode-current feedback values.
6. Repeat with known input values across the approved operating range.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system starts successfully.
2. Verify both ADC chip-select signals are inactive while idle.
3. Verify both ADC channels are sampled without requiring blocking application processing.
4. Verify a valid paired feedback result is published.
5. Verify high-voltage and cathode-current values are available.
6. Verify the published values are within the approved measurement tolerance.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-10
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-11
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-36
TITLE: External ADC invalid-result handling - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall reject external ADC results containing framing, DMA, or
acquisition-timing errors and shall not use an invalid result for feedback
processing.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and operating with valid external ADC feedback.
* A bus or firmware fault-injection method is available.
* Feedback result status or equivalent diagnostic logging is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Capture a valid external ADC result.
2. Inject an invalid ADC framing condition.
3. Repeat with an ADC DMA-transfer error.
4. Repeat with an ADC completion-timing failure.
5. Observe the result status and feedback-control outputs.
6. Restore valid ADC communication and capture the next result.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the valid result is accepted.
2. Verify the framing error is reported as invalid.
3. Verify the DMA error is reported as invalid.
4. Verify the timing failure is reported as invalid.
5. Verify invalid feedback is not used for feedback processing or output control.
6. Verify valid feedback processing resumes after communication is restored.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-10
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-11
  ROLE: Verifies

